The module is now implemented around the theorem’s “good pair” witness: an answer is the ordered set of selection-vertex IDs, and verification recomputes every incidence constraint without consulting the plant. The rendered medium instance is about 15 KB, with 136 selected IDs and a structure-aware label space of \(16^{16}\); I’m running the full 200,000-guess, attack, scaling, and relabelling suite now.
